Teserra is a C++20 game engine in development: https://github.com/fyernald/teserra

$description

Running it
----------
1. Unpack the archive anywhere, then open a terminal in its folder.
2. Run ./$executable
3. Press Escape or close the window to quit.

If your archive tool dropped the executable bit, restore it with chmod +x $executable. The program does not
install anything and only writes teserra.log into this folder.

Requirements: 64-bit Ubuntu 24.04 or 26.04 LTS (other distributions from 2024 on should work too), an X11 or
Wayland desktop, and a graphics driver with OpenGL 4.5 (Mesa 24 or newer, or a current NVIDIA or AMD
driver). Sound plays through PulseAudio, PipeWire or ALSA; without a sound device it runs silently.

Feedback
--------
Please tell us whether it worked, even if it did:
$feedback_url

Useful to include: what you saw, your distribution and desktop (X11 or Wayland), your GPU and driver version,
and the teserra.log file from this folder (it lists the GPU and OpenGL version and any error).

